IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg10-sos-service`
IMPORT `dg10-suits`
IMPORT `dg10-close-status`
IMPORT `dg10-close-governance`
IMPORT `dg10-pbc`
IMPORT `dg10-foreign-qualification`
IMPORT `dg10-foreign-withdrawal-and-suits`
IMPORT `dg10-seat`

-- WORKED CASES for dg10-seat.l4 (Delaware General Corporation Law, Subchapters XIII to XVI, ss 321-385).
-- One case at least for every question in the seat layer, with the facts a real person in the seat would state, and
-- cases outside the encoding (NOTHING) where a question can answer "not covered".
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text (src:1632-1934) beside the assertion, before the run; none
-- is copied from the encoding's own output. The inputs of each call are in the order of the question's GIVEN.

§ `Fixtures`

`dg10 case way officer` MEANS `a copy delivered personally in this State to an officer or director under s 321(a)`
`dg10 case way agent` MEANS `a copy delivered personally in this State to the registered agent under s 321(a)`
`dg10 case way abode` MEANS `a copy left at the dwelling house or usual place of abode in this State of an officer, director or individual registered agent under s 321(a)`
`dg10 case way office` MEANS `a copy left at the registered office of the corporation in this State under s 321(a)`
`dg10 case way unlisted` MEANS `a way of service that s 321(a) does not list`

`dg10 case route 321` MEANS `service on a Delaware corporation under s 321(b)`
`dg10 case route 376` MEANS `service on a qualified foreign corporation under s 376(b)`
`dg10 case route 381` MEANS `service on a foreign corporation that has withdrawn, under s 381(c) and (d)`
`dg10 case route 382` MEANS `service on a foreign corporation that never qualified, under s 382(a) and (c)`

§ `Suits against my corporation, its directors, officers or stockholders (s 321 to s 330)`

-- s 321. Process left with an officer in person is good service.
#ASSERT `Has process been validly served on my corporation` `dg10 case way officer` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 2) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A copy left at the registered office on 1 March, return date 7 March, an adult present, the manner stated in the
-- return: delivered 6 days before the return date, in time.
#ASSERT `Has process been validly served on my corporation` `dg10 case way office` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 7) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Left on 2 March, 5 days before: too late.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has process been validly served on my corporation` `dg10 case way office` (YMD 2027 3 2) (YMD 2027 3 7) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Process returnable forthwith must be delivered personally: a copy left at an abode will not do.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has process been validly served on my corporation` `dg10 case way abode` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2027 3 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Has process been validly served on my corporation` `dg10 case way agent` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Not served in a way (a) lists, but the server could not serve by due diligence and served the Secretary of State.
#ASSERT `Has process been validly served on my corporation` `dg10 case way unlisted` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 7) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- ... by electronic transmission the Secretary of State has not prescribed: not good.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has process been validly served on my corporation` `dg10 case way unlisted` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 7) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Another statute or rule of court (s 3111 of Title 10).
#ASSERT `Has process been validly served on my corporation` `dg10 case way unlisted` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 7) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has process been validly served on my corporation` `dg10 case way unlisted` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 7) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- The Secretary of State's letter (inputs: route, sent forthwith, by mail or courier with proof, enclosed the
-- process, an address appears, to principal place, to last registered office, to the certificate's address, to the
-- plaintiff's address).
#ASSERT `Is the Secretary of State's letter to my corporation what the statute requires` `dg10 case route 321` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- No address on the records: the last registered office.
#ASSERT `Is the Secretary of State's letter to my corporation what the statute requires` `dg10 case route 321` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- An address appears but the letter went to the registered office: not what s 321(b) requires.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Secretary of State's letter to my corporation what the statute requires` `dg10 case route 321` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Not forthwith.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Secretary of State's letter to my corporation what the statute requires` `dg10 case route 321` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is the Secretary of State's letter to my corporation what the statute requires` `dg10 case route 376` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the Secretary of State's letter to my corporation what the statute requires` `dg10 case route 381` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Secretary of State's letter to my corporation what the statute requires` `dg10 case route 381` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is the Secretary of State's letter to my corporation what the statute requires` `dg10 case route 382` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Secretary of State's letter to my corporation what the statute requires` `dg10 case route 382` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- The plaintiff's steps (inputs: route, duplicate, notified, amount paid, fee prescribed).
#ASSERT `As plaintiff, have I done what I must when serving a corporation through the Secretary of State` `dg10 case route 321` TRUE TRUE 75 75
#ASSERT NOT (`As plaintiff, have I done what I must when serving a corporation through the Secretary of State` `dg10 case route 321` TRUE TRUE 74 75)
#ASSERT `As plaintiff, have I done what I must when serving a corporation through the Secretary of State` `dg10 case route 376` TRUE TRUE 75 75
#ASSERT `As plaintiff, have I done what I must when serving a corporation through the Secretary of State` `dg10 case route 381` TRUE TRUE 80 75
#ASSERT NOT (`As plaintiff, have I done what I must when serving a corporation through the Secretary of State` `dg10 case route 382` FALSE TRUE 75 75)
#ASSERT NOT (`As plaintiff, have I done what I must when serving a corporation through the Secretary of State` `dg10 case route 382` TRUE FALSE 75 75)
-- The fee is taxed as costs if I prevail.
#ASSERT `If I win, will the fee I paid the Secretary of State be taxed as part of the costs` `dg10 case route 321` TRUE
#ASSERT `If I win, will the fee I paid the Secretary of State be taxed as part of the costs` `dg10 case route 376` TRUE
#ASSERT `If I win, will the fee I paid the Secretary of State be taxed as part of the costs` `dg10 case route 381` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`If I win, will the fee I paid the Secretary of State be taxed as part of the costs` `dg10 case route 382` FALSE)
-- Record retention: received 15 January 2020; the fifth anniversary is inside, the next day outside.
#ASSERT `Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service of process on my corporation` `dg10 case route 321` (YMD 2020 1 15) (YMD 2025 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service of process on my corporation` `dg10 case route 321` (YMD 2020 1 15) (YMD 2025 1 16))
#ASSERT `Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service of process on my corporation` `dg10 case route 376` (YMD 2020 1 15) (YMD 2022 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service of process on my corporation` `dg10 case route 381` (YMD 2020 1 15) (YMD 2025 1 16))
#ASSERT `Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service of process on my corporation` `dg10 case route 382` (YMD 2020 1 15) (YMD 2025 1 15)

-- s 322. A Delaware corporation that ignores a court order: a receiver of the corporation.
#ASSERT `Can the Court of Chancery appoint a receiver for my corporation because it did not obey a court order` TRUE `this State` EQUALS `a receiver of the corporation under s 322`
-- A foreign corporation: a receiver of its assets within this State.
#ASSERT `Can the Court of Chancery appoint a receiver for my corporation because it did not obey a court order` TRUE `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` EQUALS `a receiver of the assets of the corporation within this State under s 322`
#ASSERT `Can the Court of Chancery appoint a receiver for my corporation because it did not obey a court order` FALSE `this State` EQUALS `no receiver on the ground in s 322`

-- s 323. 30 days of ignoring a peremptory writ of mandamus (inputs: days, party in interest, prepared by me).
#ASSERT `As a party in interest, may I file a statement with the Attorney General because the corporation ignored a writ of mandamus` 30 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`As a party in interest, may I file a statement with the Attorney General because the corporation ignored a writ of mandamus` 29 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`As a party in interest, may I file a statement with the Attorney General because the corporation ignored a writ of mandamus` 45 FALSE TRUE)
-- The charter may be decreed forfeited after the statement, on competent proof and proper proceedings.
#ASSERT `Can the court decree my corporation's charter forfeited because it ignored a writ of mandamus` 30 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the court decree my corporation's charter forfeited because it ignored a writ of mandamus` 30 TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the court decree my corporation's charter forfeited because it ignored a writ of mandamus` 29 TRUE TRUE)

-- s 324(a). My shares attached for my debt (inputs: debt, on the books, uncertificated, s 8-112 satisfied).
#ASSERT `Can my shares, option, right or interest in a corporation be attached for my debt` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my shares, option, right or interest in a corporation be attached for my debt` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my shares, option, right or interest in a corporation be attached for my debt` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my shares, option, right or interest in a corporation be attached for my debt` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my shares, option, right or interest in a corporation be attached for my debt` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- An order of sale (inputs: uncertificated, s 8-112, final judgment, notice as for execution sales).
#ASSERT `Can an order for the sale of my attached shares issue now` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can an order for the sale of my attached shares issue now` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can an order for the sale of my attached shares issue now` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Can an order for the sale of my attached shares issue now` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Debt 1000, interest 50, costs 20: the sale has produced 1070.
#ASSERT `Has enough of my shares been sold to cover the debt, interest and costs, so that no more may be sold` 1000 50 20 1070
#ASSERT NOT (`Has enough of my shares been sold to cover the debt, interest and costs, so that no more may be sold` 1000 50 20 1069)
-- Notice of the sale (inputs: live out of the county, nonresident, mailed, newspaper exists, published there,
-- times, weeks, published in the process county, days before the sale).
#ASSERT `Was the notice of the sale of my shares by mail and publication sufficient` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0
#ASSERT `Was the notice of the sale of my shares by mail and publication sufficient` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 1 FALSE 10
#ASSERT NOT (`Was the notice of the sale of my shares by mail and publication sufficient` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 1 FALSE 9)
#ASSERT `Was the notice of the sale of my shares by mail and publication sufficient` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 2 2 TRUE 10
#ASSERT NOT (`Was the notice of the sale of my shares by mail and publication sufficient` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 1 2 TRUE 10)
-- My transfer after attachment is void once the shares are sold.
#ASSERT `Is my transfer of the shares void because it was made after attachment and the shares were sold` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my transfer of the shares void because it was made after attachment and the shares were sold` FALSE TRUE)
-- Sold, but my transfer was made before the attachment: not void under this subsection.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my transfer of the shares void because it was made after attachment and the shares were sold` TRUE FALSE)

-- s 324(b). Attachment process served on the corporation 1 March 2027: 20 days.
#ASSERT `By what date must my corporation serve its certificate of the debtor's shares on the plaintiff` (YMD 2027 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 3 21)
#ASSERT `Has my corporation served the certificate on the plaintiff in time and with what is required` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 21) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation served the certificate on the plaintiff in time and with what is required` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 22) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- On time but the certificate does not give the number of shares with their distinguishing marks.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation served the certificate on the plaintiff in time and with what is required` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaws cannot excuse the corporation.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a provision of my corporation's certificate of incorporation or bylaws excuse it from serving the certificate on the plaintiff` `in the certificate of incorporation`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a provision of my corporation's certificate of incorporation or bylaws excuse it from serving the certificate on the plaintiff` `in the bylaws`)

-- s 324(c). The purchaser (inputs: sale made and confirmed, certified copy left, there is a certificate, it was left).
#ASSERT `Is the purchaser at the sale of my attached shares entitled to the shares, option, right or interest` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the purchaser at the sale of my attached shares entitled to the shares, option, right or interest` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the purchaser at the sale of my attached shares entitled to the shares, option, right or interest` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is the purchaser entitled to a dividend that was declared or became payable after the attachment` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the purchaser entitled to a dividend that was declared or became payable after the attachment` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does the sale transfer my shares to the purchaser even though my corporation's certificate of incorporation or bylaws restrict transfer` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the sale transfer my shares to the purchaser even though my corporation's certificate of incorporation or bylaws restrict transfer` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can the court make my corporation issue new certificates or uncertificated shares to the purchaser and cancel the registration of the attached shares` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the court make my corporation issue new certificates or uncertificated shares to the purchaser and cancel the registration of the attached shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 324(d)
#ASSERT `Is the money from the sale of my shares applied as the law of attachment of personal property directs` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the money from the sale of my shares applied as the law of attachment of personal property directs` FALSE)

-- s 325 (inputs: I am an officer, director or stockholder; the Law makes me liable; the creditor is owed by me;
-- judgment against the corporation; execution returned unsatisfied).
#ASSERT `Can a creditor sue me personally, as an officer, director or stockholder, for a debt of the corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- No judgment against the corporation yet: not yet.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a creditor sue me personally, as an officer, director or stockholder, for a debt of the corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Judgment but execution not returned unsatisfied: not yet.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a creditor sue me personally, as an officer, director or stockholder, for a debt of the corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- No provision of the chapter makes me liable.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a creditor sue me personally, as an officer, director or stockholder, for a debt of the corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a creditor sue me personally, as an officer, director or stockholder, for a debt of the corporation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Does the complaint I file against officers, directors or stockholders state what the Law requires` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the complaint I file against officers, directors or stockholders state what the Law requires` TRUE FALSE)

-- s 326
#ASSERT `Can I recover from the corporation a corporate debt that I paid` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I recover from the corporation a corporate debt that I paid` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `How much can I recover from the corporation for a debt of the corporation that I paid` TRUE 12500 EQUALS JUST 12500
#ASSERT `How much can I recover from the corporation for a debt of the corporation that I paid` FALSE 12500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `In my action against the corporation for a debt I paid, can this property be taken` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`In my action against the corporation for a debt I paid, can this property be taken` FALSE)

-- s 327
#ASSERT `In my derivative suit, can my complaint make the averment of stock ownership the Law requires` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `In my derivative suit, can my complaint make the averment of stock ownership the Law requires` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`In my derivative suit, can my complaint make the averment of stock ownership the Law requires` FALSE FALSE)

-- s 328
#ASSERT `Is the liability of my corporation, or the remedies of its creditors, lessened by this transaction` TRUE `a merger or consolidation of the corporation with 1 or more corporations under s 328` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the liability of my corporation, or the remedies of its creditors, lessened by this transaction` TRUE `a change or amendment in the certificate of incorporation under s 328` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A transaction the section does not list: not covered.
#ASSERT `Is the liability of my corporation, or the remedies of its creditors, lessened by this transaction` TRUE `an event that s 328 does not list` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A corporation not of this State: not covered.
#ASSERT `Is the liability of my corporation, or the remedies of its creditors, lessened by this transaction` FALSE `a sale of the assets of the corporation under s 328` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 329
#ASSERT `Can this party assert that the corporation was not legally organized as a defense to a claim` `a corporation of this State under s 329(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can this party assert that the corporation was not legally organized as a defense to a claim` `a person sued by a corporation of this State under s 329(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can this party assert that the corporation was not legally organized as a defense to a claim` `another party under s 329(a)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can a court inquire into the regularity of my corporation's organization or its possession of a power it asserts, and hear evidence on it` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a court inquire into the regularity of my corporation's organization or its possession of a power it asserts, and hear evidence on it` TRUE FALSE)

-- s 330
#ASSERT `Can my corporation plead a usury statute against its own bond, note or other evidence of indebtedness` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A suit on some other debt: not covered.
#ASSERT `Can my corporation plead a usury statute against its own bond, note or other evidence of indebtedness` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `My close corporation (s 341 to s 356)`

-- s 341. A close corporation is governed by the chapter including the subchapter.
#ASSERT `Is the close corporation subchapter part of the law that governs my corporation` TRUE EQUALS `this chapter, including this subchapter, under s 341(a)`
-- A corporation that has not elected is subject to the chapter except the subchapter.
#ASSERT `Is the close corporation subchapter part of the law that governs my corporation` FALSE EQUALS `this chapter, except this subchapter, under s 341(a)`
-- s 341(b). The chapter applies to a close corporation unless the subchapter provides otherwise on the point.
#ASSERT `On this point, does the General Corporation Law apply to my close corporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `On this point, does the General Corporation Law apply to my close corporation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a close corporation: subsection (b) says nothing.
#ASSERT `On this point, does the General Corporation Law apply to my close corporation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 342(a). All seven facts hold, with 30 holders at most: a close corporation.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation a close corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 30 TRUE TRUE
-- 31 holders exceeds the ceiling of 30 in s 342(a)(1).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation a close corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 31 TRUE TRUE)
-- Stock not all represented by certificates.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation a close corporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 TRUE TRUE)
-- No transfer restriction.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation a close corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10 FALSE TRUE)
-- Public offering not excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation a close corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10 TRUE FALSE)
-- The s 102 contents are missing.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation a close corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 10 TRUE TRUE)
-- Not organized under the Law.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation a close corporation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10 TRUE TRUE)
-- No number of holders is specified at all.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation a close corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 10 TRUE TRUE)

-- s 342(b). The certificate names classes entitled and I am in one of them.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled under the certificate of incorporation to be a holder of record of this stock` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- It names classes entitled and I am not in one of them.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled under the certificate of incorporation to be a holder of record of this stock` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- It names classes not entitled and I am in one of them.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled under the certificate of incorporation to be a holder of record of this stock` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- It names classes not entitled and I am not in one of them.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled under the certificate of incorporation to be a holder of record of this stock` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- It sets no qualifications: nothing disqualifies me.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled under the certificate of incorporation to be a holder of record of this stock` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- It names both lists, I am in the entitled list and also in the list not entitled.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled under the certificate of incorporation to be a holder of record of this stock` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

-- s 342(c). 5 holders hold singly and 2 joint tenancies hold: 7 stockholders.
#ASSERT `How many holders of record does my close corporation have, counting joint holdings as one` 5 2 EQUALS 7
-- Three people in a joint tenancy count as one stockholder: 1 single holder plus 1 tenancy is 2.
#ASSERT `How many holders of record does my close corporation have, counting joint holdings as one` 1 1 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Is my close corporation's stock held of record by more persons than its certificate allows` 5 2 6
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my close corporation's stock held of record by more persons than its certificate allows` 5 2 7)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my close corporation's stock held of record by more persons than its certificate allows` 3 0 30)
#ASSERT `Is my close corporation's stock held of record by more persons than its certificate allows` 20 11 30

-- s 343. Formed under ss 101 to 103, with the heading and the s 342 contents.
#ASSERT `Was my close corporation formed as the Law requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 30 TRUE TRUE
-- No close corporation heading.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my close corporation formed as the Law requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 30 TRUE TRUE)
-- Not formed in accordance with ss 101 to 103.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my close corporation formed as the Law requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 30 TRUE TRUE)
-- The certificate lacks the s 342 contents (31 holders).
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my close corporation formed as the Law requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 31 TRUE TRUE)

-- s 344. Certificate of amendment complete, adopted under s 242; 200 of 300 shares approved is exactly 2/3.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation become a close corporation by electing to` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 200 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 199 of 300 is less than 2/3.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation become a close corporation by electing to` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 199 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The heading is missing.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation become a close corporation by electing to` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 300 300 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The statement of election is missing.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation become a close corporation by electing to` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 300 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not adopted under s 241 or s 242.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation become a close corporation by electing to` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 300 300 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A class with no shares outstanding gives no proportion to test.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation become a close corporation by electing to` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 345. A close corporation stays one when nothing has deleted the provisions and no breach is unremedied.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation continue to be a close corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Breach unremedied.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation continue to be a close corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Breach but the s 348 steps were taken.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation continue to be a close corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- A certificate of amendment deleting the provisions was filed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation continue to be a close corporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Not a close corporation to begin with.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation continue to be a close corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 346(b). The certificate sets 75 percent: three quarters is required.
#ASSERT `What proportion of a class of stock must approve ending our close corporation status, or amending the provision that sets a greater vote` TRUE 75 EQUALS 0.75
-- No greater vote: 2/3.
#ASSERT `What proportion of a class of stock must approve ending our close corporation status, or amending the provision that sets a greater vote` FALSE 0 EQUALS (2 DIVIDED BY 3)
-- The certificate asks for a lesser figure (50 percent), so 2/3 still governs.
#ASSERT `What proportion of a class of stock must approve ending our close corporation status, or amending the provision that sets a greater vote` TRUE 50 EQUALS (2 DIVIDED BY 3)
-- All shares of the class.
#ASSERT `What proportion of a class of stock must approve ending our close corporation status, or amending the provision that sets a greater vote` TRUE 100 EQUALS 1

-- s 346(a). Adopted under s 242, 200 of 300 approved, no greater vote.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation voluntarily ended its close corporation status` TRUE 300 200 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has my corporation voluntarily ended its close corporation status` TRUE 300 199 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Greater vote of 90 percent: 270 of 300 is enough, 269 is not.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation voluntarily ended its close corporation status` TRUE 300 270 TRUE 90 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has my corporation voluntarily ended its close corporation status` TRUE 300 269 TRUE 90 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A lesser figure in the certificate (50 percent) does not lower the 2/3.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation voluntarily ended its close corporation status` TRUE 300 199 TRUE 50 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has my corporation voluntarily ended its close corporation status` TRUE 300 200 TRUE 50 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Unanimity required: 299 of 300 is not enough.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation voluntarily ended its close corporation status` TRUE 300 299 TRUE 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not adopted and effective under s 242.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation voluntarily ended its close corporation status` FALSE 300 300 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No shares outstanding in the class.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation voluntarily ended its close corporation status` TRUE 0 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 347(a). I am not eligible and the certificate conspicuously notes who may hold.
#ASSERT `As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that I am not eligible to be a holder of this stock` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that I am not eligible to be a holder of this stock` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that I am not eligible to be a holder of this stock` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 347(b). The certificate states 10 and says so conspicuously; after the transfer 11 would hold.
#ASSERT `As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that the transfer puts the stock in more hands than the certificate allows` TRUE 10 TRUE 11
#ASSERT NOT (`As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that the transfer puts the stock in more hands than the certificate allows` TRUE 10 TRUE 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that the transfer puts the stock in more hands than the certificate allows` TRUE 10 FALSE 11)
#ASSERT NOT (`As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that the transfer puts the stock in more hands than the certificate allows` FALSE 10 TRUE 11)
-- A stated number over 30 is not within the section.
#ASSERT NOT (`As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that the transfer puts the stock in more hands than the certificate allows` TRUE 31 TRUE 32)
-- s 347(c)
#ASSERT `As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that I acquired the stock in breach of a transfer restriction` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that I acquired the stock in breach of a transfer restriction` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that I acquired the stock in breach of a transfer restriction` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`As a transferee, am I presumed to have notice that I acquired the stock in breach of a transfer restriction` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 347(d) and (e). Notice of ineligibility, no consent, no s 346 amendment.
#ASSERT `May the close corporation refuse to register the transfer of the stock into my name` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May the close corporation refuse to register the transfer of the stock into my name` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May the close corporation refuse to register the transfer of the stock into my name` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the close corporation refuse to register the transfer of the stock into my name` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- All stockholders consented.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the close corporation refuse to register the transfer of the stock into my name` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- The corporation amended its certificate under s 346.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the close corporation refuse to register the transfer of the stock into my name` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 347(f). A gift is a transfer.
#ASSERT `Does section 347 cover a transfer of stock that was not for value, such as a gift` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 347 cover a transfer of stock that was not for value, such as a gift` FALSE)
-- s 347(g). I have a right to rescind: the section does not impair it.
#ASSERT `Does section 347 take away my right to rescind the transfer or to recover under a warranty` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 347 take away my right to rescind the transfer or to recover under a warranty` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 348(a)(1). Event and discovery both on 1 March 2027: 30 days after is 31 March.
#ASSERT `By what date must my close corporation file a certificate after a breach to keep its status` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 3 31)
-- Discovered later, on 10 March: 30 days after discovery is 9 April.
#ASSERT `By what date must my close corporation file a certificate after a breach to keep its status` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2027 4 9)
-- Event 1 January 2027, discovered 15 March 2027: 14 April.
#ASSERT `By what date must my close corporation file a certificate after a breach to keep its status` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2027 3 15) EQUALS (YMD 2027 4 14)
-- Discovered before the event (a mistaken date): the later of the two periods governs.
#ASSERT `By what date must my close corporation file a certificate after a breach to keep its status` (YMD 2027 3 20) (YMD 2027 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 4 19)

-- s 348(a). Filed on 31 March 2027, the 30th day; stated, executed, furnished, and the correction made.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation keep its status as a close corporation after the breach` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 31) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Filed on 1 April 2027, the 31st day: too late.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation keep its status as a close corporation after the breach` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 4 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No copy furnished to each stockholder.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation keep its status as a close corporation after the breach` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 20) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The situation was not corrected.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation keep its status as a close corporation after the breach` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 20) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The certificate does not say the provision has ceased to apply.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation keep its status as a close corporation after the breach` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 20) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Discovered 10 March, filed 8 April (28 days after discovery, 38 after the event): in time.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation keep its status as a close corporation after the breach` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 10) (YMD 2027 4 8) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

